            <ArticleTitle>Using work simulation to treat adults with back injuries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Occupational therapy at the Liberty Mutual Medical Service Center, Boston, Massachusetts, offers a diverse variety of modalities for the treatment of patients with low back pain. Treatment may include the use of a balance monitor, a multiwork station, a pneumatic lifting-lowering device, a computerized upper extremity work simulator, and a truck-driving simulator. The primary objective of occupational therapy in this setting is to provide a supportive environment where patients can practice and improve the execution of the work-related activities they need to perform their jobs while they are learning to live with or control their symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
